{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And Moses.</b> Even though they performed all the aforementioned signs, his heart did not soften to send them, for HaShem hardened it. And it would have been fitting for the section \"And it came to pass at midnight\" to come after this, since the plagues follow in order; only the section \"This month\" was inserted in the middle, to make known how the firstborn of Israel were spared when the destroyer came upon the Egyptians."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:22.625801290Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}